content:
**Rule.** Every bill credit on an Electric Service by Rate Schedule account carries the reason for the credit and the reference of the record it comes from, and its amount is taken from that record. The reasons are:

- a security deposit refund, or a deposit applied to the balance;
- deposit interest;
- a capital credit retirement, or a capital credit offset;
- arrears moved to a PrePay Power or payment arrangement record;
- a remaining prepaid balance moved back from PrePay Power;
- a late-charge waiver;
- a meter error refund;
- a billing error correction;
- an area light outage credit.

**One credit per source and reason.** One source record yields at most one credit for the same reason. A second credit with the same source and the same reason is not posted.

**Billing error corrections.** A billing error correction is posted only for a charge line shown to be billed at the wrong schedule or quantity, and for the difference only.

### Cases (hypothetical)

| Case | Result |
|---|---|
| A late payment charge already carries a late-charge waiver credit, and a second waiver credit for the same charge is proposed | Not posted |
| A deposit carries a deposit interest credit and is later applied to the balance | Both may be posted — the reasons differ |
| An energy line billed at the Schedule GS-1 rate on an account assigned Schedule R | A billing error correction for the difference between the two pricings only |
| A member disputes a bill as too high with no line shown billed at the wrong schedule or quantity | No billing error correction |
